  I'm sorry, but that's not really ;-) accurate.  (First off, lifri means to
experience something, not to live.  jmive is "alive").  To say something
"isn't really" x implies that it has x-ish qualities, or in other words, IS
x-ish to some extent.  "other-than-" is a better translation of na'e (or
even just plain "not-", but understood to be referring to just the immediate
following brivla, nothing else).

